lesson: 121
title: Adding across ten
level: primary-1
stars: 0
explain: When two numbers together make more than ten, first fill up a ten, then add what is left.
explain: 8 + 5: take 2 of the 5 to make 8 + 2 = 10, then add the other 3: 10 + 3 = 13.
vars: a=name b=name t=thing x=2..9 y=2..9
need: x + y > 10
answer: x + y
exercise: {a} has {x} {t}. {a.He} gets {y} more. How many {t} does {a.he} have now?
exercise: There are {x} {t} in a box and {y} {t} on the table. How many {t} are there in all?
exercise: {a} found {x} {t} in the morning and {y} {t} in the afternoon. How many {t} did {a.he} find altogether?
exercise: What is {x} plus {y}?
exercise: {a} has {x} {t} and {b} has {y} {t}. How many {t} do they have together?
exercise: {x} {t} are on one shelf and {y} {t} are on another. How many {t} are on the two shelves?
test: How many {t} are there when {y} {t} are added to {x} {t}?
test: {b} gives {a} {y} {t}. Before that {a} had {x} {t}. How many {t} does {a} have now?
test: A bag holds {x} big {t} and {y} small {t}. How many {t} are in the bag?
test: Find the sum of {x} and {y}.
exercise: {a} has {x} {t} and is given {y} more. How many {t} does {a.he} have in total?
exercise: In a classroom in Leeds there are {x} {t} in a box and {y} {t} on the desk. How many {t} are there altogether?
exercise: How many {t} did {a} find in all, if {a.he} found {x} in the morning and {y} in the afternoon?
exercise: Add {x} and {y}.
exercise: {a} and {b} put their {t} together: {a} has {x.words} and {b} has {y.words}. How many {t} do they have combined?
exercise: What is {x.words} plus {y.words}?
exercise: There are {x} {t} on the top shelf and {y} {t} on the bottom shelf. How many {t} are on both shelves together?
exercise: {a} was given {x} {t} on Saturday and {y} {t} on Sunday. How many {t} did {a.he} get over the weekend?
test: {y} {t} and {x} {t} make how many {t}?
test: {a} had {x} {t}. Then {a.his} gran in Cork sent {a.him} {y} more. How many {t} has {a} got now?
test: How many {t} are in a basket with {x} new {t} and {y} old {t}?
test: Increase {x} by {y}. What number do you get?
test: What is the total of {x} and {y}?
test: {b} brings {y} {t} to school in Adelaide, and {a} brings {x} {t}. Altogether, how many {t} did the two of them bring?
exercise: got {x} {t}, mum gave me {y} more. how many now
exercise: {a} had {x+1}, no wait, {x} {t}, then {b} gave {a.him} {y}. how many {a.he} got
exercise: {b} says {x} + {y} is {x+y-1}. that's wrong innit, what is it
exercise: {x} {t} in my bag n {y} in my pocket, school bus was 10 mins late btw. how many altogether
test: {x} plus {y} whats that
test: {a} found {x+2}, nah, {x} {t} this morning and {y} in the arvo. how many all up
test: my mate reckons {x} n {y} makes {x+y+1}?? nah, how many {t} is it really
exam: It is given that {a} is in possession of {x.words} {t} and subsequently receives a further {y.words}. Determine the aggregate quantity of {t} so held.
exam: Whereas a box contains {x} {t} and a table bears {y} {t}, ascertain the total number of {t} present.
exam: {a} located {x} {t} during the forenoon and {y} {t} during the afternoon. State the cardinality of the set of {t} so located.
exam: Compute the sum of {x.words} and {y.words}.
exercise: Grandma passed away and left {a} her {x} stamps. {a}'s aunt finds {y} more stamps in the attic and gives them to {a}. How many stamps does {a} have now?
exercise: {a} fibbed and said {a.he} had no {t}. Really {a.he} had {x}, and then {b} gave {a.him} {y} more. How many {t} does {a} really have now?
test: nan "went to a better place" and her {x} {t} came to us. we had {y} already. how many now, quick, dont just stand there
